<section id="syntax">
  <h2>Writing entries</h2>

  <p>
    Type what you have <b>DONE</b> and press Enter. Markup anywhere in the line adds tags and times, but is completely optional.
    The text is always saved the way you typed it.
  </p>

  <p>
    Feel free to add <b>TODO</b>s for the coming days. Or copy a task you didn't finish and left as <b>DOING</b> to the next day. It's all up to you, we won't take assumptions how you want to use your data.
  </p>

  <h3>Working time</h3>

  <p>
    Working time is between <code>start@</code> and <code>end@</code> minus the <code>#break</code> durations. Logging
    <% SyntaxGuide::DAY.each do |log| %><code><%= log %></code> <% end %>
    on one line or as separate entries adds up to <strong><%= SyntaxGuide::DAY_TOTAL %></strong>.
  </p>

  <p>
    A duration from <code>for~</code> or <code>from@</code> / <code>to@</code> counts for the one <b>#tag</b> on the same line.
    These tag times are for reports only (<b>tag times</b> on the project page), they never change the working time.
  </p>

  <%= render "help/syntax_table" %>

  <p id="times-optional">
    <i>Logging times is optional.</i> Unless you use <b>done</b> for time tracking, then you can configure your projects to require and
    <b>validate</b> your entries for proper time logging.
  </p>

  <h3>What stays plain text</h3>

  <ul>
    <% SyntaxGuide::NOT_MARKUP.each do |example| %>
      <li><code><%= example.log %></code> &mdash; <%= example.meaning %></li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
</section>
